    "result_text": "Done. The full configured test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{id}` response is an `OwnerDto` generated from `openapi.yml` and populated by MapStruct from the `Owner` entity \u2014 the same pattern used by the existing derived fields (`membershipNumber`, `initials`, `displayName`). I followed that convention with two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getMembershipTier()`:\n   ```java\n   boolean unique = this.namesakeCount != null && this.namesakeCount == 0;\n   boolean hasEmail = this.email != null && !this.email.isBlank();\n   return unique && hasEmail ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\";\n   ```\n\n2. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct auto-maps it from the getter.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest` (both `coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail` and `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) pass, and `./mvnw test` reports `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
