    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe new `getMembershipTier()` is placed correctly and follows the codebase's existing conventions:\n\n- **Right unit**: The tier is derived purely from the owner's own fields (`namesakeCount`, `email`), so a computed getter on `Owner` is the natural home. It sits directly alongside an existing derived `@Transient` getter (the `customerCode`/`registrationDate` formatting method), matching the established pattern for derived read-only properties on this entity.\n- **No duplication / not a catch-all**: Owner already hosts these derived accessors, so this is additive and consistent rather than turning the class into a dumping ground.\n- **Idiomatic**: `@Transient` for a non-persisted computed property, Javadoc mirroring the spec, and a corresponding `readOnly: true` field in `openapi.yml` with a matching description all align with how the rest of the model/schema are maintained.\n\nA maintainer of this Spring Boot codebase would find this placement and style natural.",
